DFlash2 speculative decoding with pipeline parallelism (heterogeneous two-GPU
setups, e.g. RTX 5070 Ti + RTX 3060 in heterogeneous/).

Upstream vLLM 0.27.1 refuses DFlash under pipeline parallelism. This patch:
- relays EAGLE3-style auxiliary hidden states across PP stage boundaries in
  qwen3_next.py (they ride in IntermediateTensors next to hidden_states and
  residual, in configured target-layer order),
- expands the intermediate-tensor factories for incoming aux states and
  refreshes the multimodal wrapper's cached factory (qwen3_5.py,
  model_runner.py),
- permits method "dflash" with PP in the V2 model runner and validates the
  complete drafter as PP-local on the last rank (config/speculative.py),
- shares the target embedding table and LM head with the drafter instead of
  allocating temporary multi-GiB BF16 copies (qwen3_dflash.py, dflash/utils.py),
- accepts the PP intermediate_tensors kwarg in DFlashSpeculator.propose and
  adds VLLM_DFLASH_CUDAGRAPH=0 to run the drafter eagerly — required here
  because the shared target LM head is Marlin-quantized and its candidate GEMM
  crashes inside DFlash's private CUDA graph capture.

Apply AFTER every other patch in this directory (the zz- prefix keeps glob
order correct):
  patch -p1 -d venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vllm < zz-dflash2-pipeline-parallel.patch

